Each glowing sphere falling from the sky is a grain of the **total net wealth of US households**, and the sand piles up in four bins. The small aligned silhouettes under each bin show the **share of the population** it stands for: 50 red figures for the poorest half, a single blue figure for the top 1%. Move the year slider, or switch on Auto-play, and watch the sand drift towards the lone blue figure.



